about:
  heading: "The Bertha Heights Estate Sale"
  paragraphs:
    - "Hidden near the top of Council Crest is the lovely Bertha Heights Estate Sale. A charming modern colonial treehouse full of vintage furniture, fine art, and other estate treasures. The estate belonged to a family of doctors that loved to collect art, religious antiques, asian furniture, and figurines from around the world. The estate is a mix of modern furniture and vintage masterpieces, from sofas and tables to cabinets and shelving. A couple grandfather clocks. There are TVs and other electronics like computers and stereos. Lots of children's books, toys and games, including a vintage train set. A walk-in closet of vintage clothes, featuring stylish designer trench coats. Avid golf enthusiasts with an array of clubs and equipment, not to mention the variety of other sporting goods and outdoor/camping goods. Lots of patio furniture and planters to fill the numerous terraces and balconies."
